{# #### `project_attributes_catering_bill_per_person_exceeding_deposit` #}

{{SetCustomerMetadataAttribute(
    idn="project_attributes_catering_bill_per_person_exceeding_deposit",
    field="multiple_fields",
    value={ "title": "5-09. ASR - Average Bill Amount For Catering Service Per Person Exceeding the Deposit
Covered Number [A]", "description": """Additional per-person charge used when guest count exceeds the deposit-covered guest limit.

**Pro-Tip:** Set this to your real incremental per-guest catering price (beyond the base deposit
package).

**Examples:**

- Higher value increases projected revenue for large catering party sizes above the covered limit.
- Lower value keeps over-limit revenue projections conservative.

---

**⚙️ Technical & System Details (Advanced)**

**System Usage:** Used directly in catering revenue formula:
`(party_size - covered_people) * per_person_excess + deposit`. Also referenced in default catering
scenario messaging for user-facing pricing explanation.

**Fallbacks:** Initialized to a catering default when empty. Runtime formula loading also applies a
numeric fallback if blank.

**Dependencies:**

- **Primary Settings:**
  - `project_business_industry`: Activates catering-specific revenue logic.
- **Logic Interactions:**
  - `project_attributes_catering_deposit`: Combined in the same formula as base charge.
  - `project_attributes_catering_deposit_covered_number_of_people`: Defines when this additional
    per-person charge starts applying.""", "group": "5. Reports", "value_type": "number", "is_hidden": False }
)}}

